  "id": "sensorimotor-memory",
  "term": "sensorimotor memory",
  "definition": "Sensorimotor memory is the short-term carryover of information from a recent action that influences how a later movement is planned and performed. In this source, it refers to remembered object weight from a previous lift, which affects predictive fingertip force scaling on a later lift and can transfer between hands.",
